IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`

-- scja2-part5-ca-capital.l4: Part 5 (Court of Appeal), Division 4, Post-appeal application in capital case and finding of abuse of process: ss 60G to 60M.
-- Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering (SCJA1969.txt), not the official text. Layer 1: the law, objectively; every name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Encoded for the prisoner awaiting capital punishment (the PACP) as the individual on whom the court acts; there is no seat export for this Division.
-- The periods that these sections leave to the Rules of Court are not among the sources: each is a plain input (a number of days), and NOTHING when it is not given.
-- The Criminal Procedure Code 2010 and the Post-appeal Applications in Capital Cases Act 2022 are not among the sources; borrowed facts are plain inputs.
-- JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (scja2)").

§ `Part 5, Division 4 -- Post-appeal application in capital case and finding of abuse of process`

§§ `s 60G -- Application for permission to make PACC application`

-- src:3605 | 60G.—(1) Subject to section 60I, before making a PACC
-- src:3606 | application, the applicant must apply to the Court of Appeal for,
-- src:3607 | and obtain, the permission of that court to do so.
@ref s 60G(1) (src:3605-3607)
GIVEN `section 60I applies to the PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the permission of the Court of Appeal to make the PACC application has been obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(1) the applicant has obtained the permission of the Court of Appeal before making the PACC application, as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 60I" -- section 60I governs where it applies
        IF `section 60I applies to the PACP` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the permission of the Court of Appeal to make the PACC application has been obtained` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "before making a PACC application, the applicant must apply to the Court of Appeal for, and obtain, the permission of that court to do so" -- a bare "must" not done: the text states the duty and does not say what follows
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 60G(1) party` IS ONE OF `s 60G(1) the applicant`
DECLARE `s 60G(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 60G(1) applies to the Court of Appeal for permission to make a PACC application`
    `s 60G(1) obtains the permission of the Court of Appeal`

-- src:3605 | 60G.—(1) Subject to section 60I, before making a PACC
-- src:3606 | application, the applicant must apply to the Court of Appeal for,
-- src:3607 | and obtain, the permission of that court to do so.
@ref s 60G(1) (src:3605-3607)
`s 60G(1) the duty of the applicant before making a PACC application` MEANS
    PARTY `s 60G(1) the applicant`
    MUST `s 60G(1) applies to the Court of Appeal for permission to make a PACC application`
    HENCE (
        PARTY `s 60G(1) the applicant`
        MUST `s 60G(1) obtains the permission of the Court of Appeal`
        LEST BREACH BY `s 60G(1) the applicant` BECAUSE "the permission of the Court of Appeal was not obtained before the PACC application was made"
    )
    LEST BREACH BY `s 60G(1) the applicant` BECAUSE "no application for permission was made before the PACC application was made"

#TRACE `s 60G(1) the duty of the applicant before making a PACC application` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 60G(1) the applicant` DOES `s 60G(1) applies to the Court of Appeal for permission to make a PACC application` AT 1
    PARTY `s 60G(1) the applicant` DOES `s 60G(1) obtains the permission of the Court of Appeal` AT 2

-- src:3609 | (2) Despite section 50(1), an application for PACC permission may
-- src:3610 | be heard and determined by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal.
@ref s 60G(2) (src:3609-3610)
GIVEN `it is an application for PACC permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(2) the application for PACC permission may be heard and determined by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal despite section 50(1)` MEANS
    IF `it is an application for PACC permission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "an application for PACC permission"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3617 | (3) An application for PACC permission must be fixed for hearing
-- src:3618 | within such period as is prescribed by the Rules of Court.
@ref s 60G(3) (src:3617-3618)
GIVEN `the period the Rules of Court prescribe for fixing the application for hearing, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of days taken to fix it for hearing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(3) the application for PACC permission is fixed for hearing within the prescribed period, as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period the Rules of Court prescribe for fixing the application for hearing, in days`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "within such period as is prescribed by the Rules of Court" -- the Rules of Court are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        IF `the number of days taken to fix it for hearing` AT MOST period
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must be fixed for hearing within such period as is prescribed" -- a bare "must" not done within a period the Rules of Court prescribe (not fixed in the text, so the period ruling does not apply): the text states the duty and does not say what follows
        ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3620 | (4) The applicant in an application for PACC permission must file
-- src:3621 | written submissions in support of that application, and such other
-- src:3622 | documents as are prescribed in the Rules of Court, within such
-- src:3623 | periods as are prescribed in the Rules of Court.
@ref s 60G(4) (src:3620-3623)
GIVEN `the period the Rules of Court prescribe for filing the written submissions and other documents, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of days taken to file them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(4) the applicant files the written submissions and other documents within the prescribed period, as the section requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period the Rules of Court prescribe for filing the written submissions and other documents, in days`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "within such periods as are prescribed in the Rules of Court" -- the Rules of Court are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        IF `the number of days taken to file them` AT MOST period
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "must file written submissions ... within such periods as are prescribed" -- a bare "must" not done within a period the Rules of Court prescribe (not fixed in the text, so the period ruling does not apply): the text states the duty and does not say what follows
        ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 60G(4) party` IS ONE OF `s 60G(4) the applicant in an application for PACC permission`
DECLARE `s 60G(4) act` IS ONE OF `s 60G(4) files written submissions in support of the application`

-- The period is the one the Rules of Court prescribe (not among the sources); the clock counts days.
-- src:3620 | (4) The applicant in an application for PACC permission must file
-- src:3621 | written submissions in support of that application, and such other
-- src:3622 | documents as are prescribed in the Rules of Court, within such
-- src:3623 | periods as are prescribed in the Rules of Court.
@ref s 60G(4) (src:3620-3623)
GIVEN period IS A NUMBER
`s 60G(4) the duty of the applicant to file written submissions` MEANS
    PARTY `s 60G(4) the applicant in an application for PACC permission`
    MUST `s 60G(4) files written submissions in support of the application`
    WITHIN period
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 60G(4) the applicant in an application for PACC permission` BECAUSE "the written submissions were not filed within the prescribed period"

#TRACE `s 60G(4) the duty of the applicant to file written submissions` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 60G(4) the applicant in an application for PACC permission` DOES `s 60G(4) files written submissions in support of the application` AT 10

-- the same duty with the submissions filed on day 20, after the 14-day period: a breach
#TRACE `s 60G(4) the duty of the applicant to file written submissions` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 60G(4) the applicant in an application for PACC permission` DOES `s 60G(4) files written submissions in support of the application` AT 20

-- src:3625 | (5) The respondent in an application for PACC permission may file
-- src:3626 | written submissions in relation to that application within such period
-- src:3627 | as is prescribed in the Rules of Court.
@ref s 60G(5) (src:3625-3627)
GIVEN `the period the Rules of Court prescribe for the respondent's written submissions, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of days taken to file them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(5) the respondent files written submissions within the prescribed period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the period the Rules of Court prescribe for the respondent's written submissions, in days`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "within such period as is prescribed in the Rules of Court" -- the Rules of Court are not among the sources
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST period THEN
        IF `the number of days taken to file them` AT MOST period
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may file written submissions ... within such period as is prescribed" -- the period has run out
        ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3629 | (6) The Registrar or any Supreme Court Judge may extend or
-- src:3630 | abridge any period mentioned in subsection (3), (4) or (5).
@ref s 60G(6) (src:3629-3630)
GIVEN `the person is the Registrar or a Supreme Court Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is one mentioned in subsection (3), (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(6) the person may extend or abridge the period` MEANS
    IF `the person is the Registrar or a Supreme Court Judge` AND `the period is one mentioned in subsection (3), (4) or (5)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is the Registrar's or a Supreme Court Judge's, over a period mentioned in subsection (3), (4) or (5)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3632 | (7) In deciding whether or not to grant an application for PACC
-- src:3633 | permission, the Court of Appeal must consider the following matters:
-- src:3635 | (a) whether the PACC application to be made is based on
-- src:3636 | material (being evidence or legal arguments) that, even
-- src:3637 | with reasonable diligence, could not have been adduced in
-- src:3638 | court before the relevant date;
-- src:3640 | (b) whether there was any delay in filing the application for
-- src:3641 | PACC permission after the PACP or counsel for the PACP
-- src:3642 | obtained the material mentioned in paragraph (a) and the
-- src:3643 | reasons for the delay;
-- src:3645 | (c) whether subsection (4) is complied with;
-- src:3647 | (d) whether the PACC application to be made has a reasonable
-- src:3648 | prospect of success.
@ref s 60G(7) (src:3632-3648)
GIVEN `it considered whether the PACC application is based on material that could not have been adduced before the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considered whether there was any delay in filing and the reasons for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considered whether subsection (4) is complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it considered whether the PACC application has a reasonable prospect of success` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(7) the Court of Appeal has considered the matters it must consider in deciding whether to grant the application, as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `it considered whether the PACC application is based on material that could not have been adduced before the relevant date`
       AND `it considered whether there was any delay in filing and the reasons for it`
       AND `it considered whether subsection (4) is complied with`
       AND `it considered whether the PACC application has a reasonable prospect of success`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "the Court of Appeal must consider the following matters: (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; (d) ..." -- one of the four is not considered -- a bare "must" not done: the text states the duty and does not say what follows
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3650 | (8) An application for PACC permission may, without being set
-- src:3651 | down for hearing, be summarily dealt with by a written order of the
-- src:3652 | Court of Appeal.
@ref s 60G(8) (src:3650-3652)
GIVEN `it is an application for PACC permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(8) the application for PACC permission may be summarily dealt with by a written order without being set down for hearing` MEANS
    IF `it is an application for PACC permission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "an application for PACC permission"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3658 | (a) must consider the applicant’s written submissions, if any;
-- src:3659 | and
@ref s 60G(9)(a) (src:3658-3659)
GIVEN `it considered the applicant's written submissions, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(9)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily refusing, as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `it considered the applicant's written submissions, if any`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Before summarily refusing ... the Court of Appeal ... (a) must consider the applicant's written submissions, if any" -- a bare "must" not done: the text states the duty and does not say what follows
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3666 | (b) may, but is not required to, consider the respondent’s
-- src:3667 | written submissions, if any.
@ref s 60G(9)(b) (src:3666-3667)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal is summarily refusing the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(9)(b) the Court of Appeal is required to consider the respondent's written submissions before summarily refusing` MEANS
    IF `the Court of Appeal is summarily refusing the application`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, but is not required to, consider the respondent's written submissions, if any"
        JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph speaks of the Court before summarily refusing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3673 | (a) must consider the applicant’s written submissions, if any;
-- src:3674 | and
@ref s 60G(10)(a) (src:3673-3674)
GIVEN `it considered the applicant's written submissions, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(10)(a) the Court of Appeal has considered the applicant's written submissions before summarily granting, as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `it considered the applicant's written submissions, if any`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Before summarily granting ... the Court of Appeal ... (a) must consider the applicant's written submissions, if any" -- a bare "must" not done: the text states the duty and does not say what follows
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3676 | (b) must consider the respondent’s written submissions, if any.
@ref s 60G(10)(b) (src:3676)
GIVEN `it considered the respondent's written submissions, if any` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(10)(b) the Court of Appeal has considered the respondent's written submissions before summarily granting, as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `it considered the respondent's written submissions, if any`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Before summarily granting ... the Court of Appeal ... (b) must consider the respondent's written submissions, if any" -- a bare "must" not done: the text states the duty and does not say what follows
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 60G(11) stage` IS ONE OF
    `s 60G(11)(a) before deciding any application for PACC permission`
    `s 60G(11)(b) when granting an application for PACC permission`
    `s 60G(11)(c) when summarily granting an application for PACC permission`
    `s 60G(11) at another stage`

DECLARE `s 60G(11) measure` IS ONE OF
    `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence`
    `s 60G(11)(e) taking additional evidence`
    `s 60G(11) another measure`

-- src:3678 | (11) The Court of Appeal may —
-- src:3680 | (a) before deciding any application for PACC permission;
-- src:3682 | (b) when granting an application for PACC permission; or
-- src:3684 | (c) when summarily granting an application for PACC
-- src:3685 | permission,
-- src:3687 | do one or both of the following:
-- src:3689 | (d) make any incidental directions or give any interim orders
-- src:3690 | (including a stay of execution of the death sentence) as the
-- src:3691 | Court considers necessary;
-- src:3693 | (e) take additional evidence.
@ref s 60G(11) (src:3678-3693)
GIVEN stage IS A `s 60G(11) stage`
      measure IS A `s 60G(11) measure`
      `the Court considers it necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(11) the Court of Appeal may take the measure at the stage` MEANS
    CONSIDER stage
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) before deciding ...; (b) when granting ...; or (c) when summarily granting ..." -- "when" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05), so a stage outside the three is the text's no (fork F-when, NOTES.md)
    WHEN `s 60G(11) at another stage` THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER measure
        WHEN `s 60G(11)(d) making an incidental direction or giving an interim order, including a stay of execution of the death sentence` THEN
            IF `the Court considers it necessary`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as the Court considers necessary"
            ELSE NOTHING
        WHEN `s 60G(11)(e) taking additional evidence` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is to do one or both of the two things in paragraphs (d) and (e)
        WHEN `s 60G(11) another measure` THEN NOTHING

-- src:3698 | (a) where the application for PACC permission is dealt with by
-- src:3699 | a single Judge of the Court of Appeal — take such
-- src:3700 | evidence itself; or
@ref s 60G(12)(a) (src:3698-3700)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Judges dealing with the application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(12)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge deals with the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (11)" -- the "if" is not met
        IF NOT `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (11)` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of Judges dealing with the application` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where the application for PACC permission is dealt with by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal" -- the "where" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:3702 | (b) where the application for PACC permission is dealt with by
-- src:3703 | 3 or any greater uneven number of Judges sitting in the
-- src:3704 | Court of Appeal — either take such evidence itself or have
-- src:3705 | such evidence taken by one of those Judges.
@ref s 60G(12)(b) (src:3702-3705)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (11)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Judges dealing with the application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(12)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (11)" -- the "if" is not met
        IF NOT `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (11)` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of Judges dealing with the application` AT LEAST 3 AND (`the number of Judges dealing with the application` MODULO 2) EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the application for PACC permission is dealt with by 3 or any greater uneven number of Judges" -- the "where" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:3707 | (13) If the Court of Appeal does not grant the application for PACC
-- src:3708 | permission, no further proceedings may be taken in respect of the
-- src:3709 | PACC application.
@ref s 60G(13) (src:3707-3709)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal does not grant the application for PACC permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(13) the bar on further proceedings in respect of the PACC application applies` MEANS
    IF `the Court of Appeal does not grant the application for PACC permission`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the Court of Appeal does not grant the application for PACC permission, no further proceedings may be taken" -- the "if" is not met (the application was granted), so the bar does not apply (ruling of 2026-11-05, part (b))
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:3716 | (14) Subsection (13) does not prevent the taking of any proceedings
-- src:3717 | against the PACP’s counsel (if any) in relation to the counsel’s
-- src:3718 | conduct in the application for PACC permission.
@ref s 60G(14) (src:3716-3718)
GIVEN `the proceedings are against the PACP's counsel in relation to the counsel's conduct in the application for PACC permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(14) subsection (13) prevents the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are against the PACP's counsel in relation to the counsel's conduct in the application for PACC permission`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (13) does not prevent the taking of any proceedings against the PACP's counsel (if any) in relation to the counsel's conduct in the application for PACC permission."
        JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of proceedings against the PACP's counsel about the counsel's conduct
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3720 | (15) Despite any provision in this section, if an application for
-- src:3721 | PACC permission is made by a PACP, and prior to the making of that
-- src:3722 | application, the applicant is found by the Court of Appeal —
-- src:3724 | (a) to have abused the process of the court in relation to a
-- src:3725 | relevant application that was filed on or after the date of
-- src:3726 | commencement of the Post‑appeal Applications in Capital
-- src:3727 | Cases Act 2022; or
-- src:3729 | (b) to have abused the process of the court in order to delay or
-- src:3730 | frustrate the carrying out of the sentence of death in
-- src:3731 | relation to an application (other than a relevant application)
-- src:3732 | or action that was filed on or after the date mentioned in
-- src:3733 | paragraph (a),
-- src:3735 | the Court of Appeal must not grant the application for PACC
-- src:3736 | permission unless —
-- src:3738 | (c) the PACP adduces material (being evidence or legal
-- src:3739 | arguments) that was not adduced in court before the date
-- src:3740 | of the most recent of any such finding of abuse of process
-- src:3741 | by the Court of Appeal; and
-- src:3743 | (d) the material could not, even with reasonable diligence,
-- src:3744 | have been adduced in court before the date mentioned in
-- src:3745 | paragraph (c).
@ref s 60G(15) (src:3720-3745)
GIVEN `the applicant was found by the Court of Appeal, before making the application, to have abused the process of the court as paragraph (a) or (b) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the PACP adduces material that was not adduced in court before the date of the most recent finding of abuse of process` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60G(15) the Court of Appeal may grant the application for PACC permission` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "if an application for PACC permission is made by a PACP, and prior to the making of that application, the applicant is found by the Court of Appeal ... to have abused the process of the court" -- the "if" is not met, so the prohibition is not triggered and the text is silent on whether the Court of Appeal may grant (that is for the rest of section 60G); the bar-phrased function below asks the prohibition's own question and answers JUST FALSE here (ruling of 2026-11-05, part (b))
        IF NOT `the applicant was found by the Court of Appeal, before making the application, to have abused the process of the court as paragraph (a) or (b) describes` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless" -- the unless is met, which lifts the bar without itself granting permission
        IF `the PACP adduces material that was not adduced in court before the date of the most recent finding of abuse of process` AND `the material could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before that date` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court of Appeal must not grant the application for PACC permission unless -- (c) ...; and (d) ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

