DECLARE `s 60I(2) what the Court of Appeal does` IS ONE OF
    `s 60I(2)(a) grants permission for the PACP to adduce further material when dealing with the specified application`
    `s 60I(2)(b) grants permission for the PACP to make the subsequent application separately under section 60G or 60H`
    `s 60I(2)(c) refuses to grant permission under paragraph (a) or (b)`
    `s 60I(2) does something else`

-- src:3835 | (2) The Court of Appeal dealing with the specified application may
-- src:3836 | do any one of the following:
-- src:3838 | (a) grant permission for the PACP to adduce further material
