GIVEN act IS A `s 60I(2) what the Court of Appeal does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60I(2) the Court of Appeal dealing with the specified application may do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 60I(2)(a) grants permission for the PACP to adduce further material when dealing with the specified application` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60I(2)(b) grants permission for the PACP to make the subsequent application separately under section 60G or 60H` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 60I(2)(c) refuses to grant permission under paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may do any one of the following" names the three things
    WHEN `s 60I(2) does something else` THEN NOTHING

