        JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER act
        WHEN `s 60J(3)(a) proceeds to determine the specified application, or that part of the specified action, in accordance with section 60G or 60H` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `s 60J(3)(b) strikes out the specified application or specified action, in whole or in part` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the two things the Court of Appeal may do
        WHEN `s 60J(3) does something else` THEN NOTHING

-- src:3892 | (4) The Court of Appeal may, in making any determination under
-- src:3893 | subsection (1), do one or both of the following:
-- src:3895 | (a) make any incidental directions or give any interim orders
-- src:3896 | (including a stay of execution of the death sentence) as the
-- src:3897 | Court considers necessary;
-- src:3899 | (b) take additional evidence.
@ref s 60J(4) (src:3892-3899)
GIVEN `it is making a determination under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60J(4) the Court of Appeal may make incidental directions, give interim orders or take additional evidence` MEANS
    IF `it is making a determination under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in making any determination under subsection (1)"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3904 | (a) where the determination under subsection (1) is being
-- src:3905 | made by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal — take such
-- src:3906 | evidence itself; or
@ref s 60J(5)(a) (src:3904-3906)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Judges making the determination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60J(5)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge makes the determination` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (4)" -- the "if" is not met
        IF NOT `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (4)` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of Judges making the determination` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where the determination under subsection (1) is being made by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal" -- the "where" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:3908 | (b) where the determination under subsection (1) is being
-- src:3909 | made by 3 or any greater uneven number of Judges sitting
-- src:3916 | in the Court of Appeal — either take such evidence itself or
-- src:3917 | have such evidence taken by one of those Judges.
@ref s 60J(5)(b) (src:3908-3917)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Judges making the determination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60J(5)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (4)" -- the "if" is not met
        IF NOT `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence needs to be taken under subsection (4)` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of Judges making the determination` AT LEAST 3 AND (`the number of Judges making the determination` MODULO 2) EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the determination under subsection (1) is being made by 3 or any greater uneven number of Judges" -- the "where" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 60K -- Operation of Division 1B of Part 20 of Criminal Procedure Code 2010`

-- src:3924 | 60K. Nothing in this Division affects the operation of Division 1B
-- src:3925 | of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010.
@ref s 60K (src:3924-3925)
GIVEN `the provision is a provision of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60K the provision affects the operation of Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010` MEANS
    IF `the provision is a provision of this Division`
    THEN
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Division affects the operation of Division 1B of Part 20 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010."
        JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of "this Division"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 60L -- Stay of execution of death sentence`

-- src:3931 | 60L. Despite anything in this Act or any other written law, a stay of
-- src:3932 | execution of the death sentence may only be granted by the Court of
-- src:3933 | Appeal.
@ref s 60L (src:3931-3933)
GIVEN court IS A Court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60L the court may grant a stay of execution of the death sentence` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a stay of execution of the death sentence may only be granted by the Court of Appeal"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 60M -- Power of Court of Appeal to make finding of abuse of process when dealing with application or action`

-- src:3940 | 60M.—(1) When dealing with any application or action, the Court
-- src:3941 | of Appeal may, on its own motion or upon the application of the
-- src:3942 | Attorney‑General or the Public Prosecutor, decide whether to make a
-- src:3943 | finding that a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP, has in the
-- src:3944 | commencement, continuation or conduct of the proceedings
-- src:3945 | relating to the application or action —
-- src:3947 | (a) committed an abuse of process, in the case of a relevant
-- src:3948 | application; or
-- src:3950 | (b) committed an abuse of process in order to delay or frustrate
-- src:3951 | the carrying out of the sentence of death imposed on the
-- src:3952 | PACP, in the case of an application (other than a relevant
-- src:3953 | application) or action.
@ref s 60M(1) (src:3940-3953)
GIVEN `it is dealing with an application or action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it acts on its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who applies` IS A MAYBE Role
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(1) the Court of Appeal may decide whether to make a finding of abuse of process` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When dealing with any application or action, the Court of Appeal may" -- "when" counts as "where" (ruling of 2026-11-05), and it is not met
        IF NOT `it is dealing with an application or action` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `it acts on its own motion` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person who applies` EQUALS JUST `Attorney-General` OR `the person who applies` EQUALS JUST `Public Prosecutor` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on its own motion or upon the application of the Attorney-General or the Public Prosecutor" -- "upon" counts as "where", and neither is met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:3947 | (a) committed an abuse of process, in the case of a relevant
-- src:3948 | application; or
@ref s 60M(1)(a) (src:3947-3948)
GIVEN `the person is a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to a relevant application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(1)(a) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in the case of a relevant application` MEANS
    IF `the person is a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP` AND `it relates to a relevant application`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the finding is about "a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP" and, in this paragraph, "a relevant application"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:3950 | (b) committed an abuse of process in order to delay or frustrate
-- src:3951 | the carrying out of the sentence of death imposed on the
-- src:3952 | PACP, in the case of an application (other than a relevant
-- src:3953 | application) or action.
@ref s 60M(1)(b) (src:3950-3953)
GIVEN `the person is a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to an application (other than a relevant application) or an action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(1)(b) the finding may be that the person committed an abuse of process in order to delay or frustrate the carrying out of the sentence of death` MEANS
    IF `the person is a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP` AND `it relates to an application (other than a relevant application) or an action`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the finding is about "a PACP, or a counsel for a PACP" and, in this paragraph, "an application (other than a relevant application) or action"
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 60M(2) kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `s 60M(2)(a) an application for PACC permission`
    `s 60M(2)(b) a PACC application`
    `s 60M(2)(c) an application for review permission`
    `s 60M(2)(d) a review application`

DECLARE `s 60M(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 60M(2)(a)(i) whether the PACC application to be made is based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`
    `s 60M(2)(a)(ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel obtained the material, and the reasons for the delay`
    `s 60M(2)(a)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 60G(4)`
    `s 60M(2)(b)(i) whether the PACC application was based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`
    `s 60M(2)(b)(ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel obtained the material, and the reasons for the delay`
    `s 60M(2)(b)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 60H(2)`
    `s 60M(2)(c)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60M(2)(c)(ii) whether the application for review permission was filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or counsel obtained the material mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60M(2)(c)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394H(3) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60M(2)(d)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60M(2)(d)(ii) whether the application for review permission granted in respect of the review application was filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or counsel obtained the material mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    `s 60M(2)(d)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394I(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`

GIVEN kind IS A `s 60M(2) kind of application`
GIVETH A LIST OF `s 60M(2) matter`
`s 60M(2) the matters that the Court of Appeal may take into account for the kind of application` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 60M(2)(a) an application for PACC permission` THEN LIST
        `s 60M(2)(a)(i) whether the PACC application to be made is based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`,
        `s 60M(2)(a)(ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel obtained the material, and the reasons for the delay`,
        `s 60M(2)(a)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 60G(4)`
    WHEN `s 60M(2)(b) a PACC application` THEN LIST
        `s 60M(2)(b)(i) whether the PACC application was based on material that could not, even with reasonable diligence, have been adduced in court before the relevant date`,
        `s 60M(2)(b)(ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel obtained the material, and the reasons for the delay`,
        `s 60M(2)(b)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 60H(2)`
    WHEN `s 60M(2)(c) an application for review permission` THEN LIST
        `s 60M(2)(c)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`,
        `s 60M(2)(c)(ii) whether the application for review permission was filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or counsel obtained the material mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`,
        `s 60M(2)(c)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394H(3) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`
    WHEN `s 60M(2)(d) a review application` THEN LIST
        `s 60M(2)(d)(i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`,
        `s 60M(2)(d)(ii) whether the application for review permission granted in respect of the review application was filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or counsel obtained the material mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`,
        `s 60M(2)(d)(iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394I(2) of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010`

-- src:3955 | (2) In deciding whether to make a finding under subsection (1), the
-- src:3956 | Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the following
-- src:3957 | matters:
-- src:3959 | (a) in relation to an application for PACC permission —
-- src:3961 | (i) whether the PACC application to be made is based on
-- src:3962 | material (being evidence or legal arguments) that,
-- src:3969 | even with reasonable diligence, could not have been
-- src:3970 | adduced in court before the relevant date;
-- src:3972 | (ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application
-- src:3973 | for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel for
-- src:3974 | the PACP obtained the material mentioned in
-- src:3975 | sub‑paragraph (i) and the reasons for the delay; and
-- src:3977 | (iii) whether the PACP has complied with
-- src:3978 | section 60G(4);
-- src:3980 | (b) in relation to a PACC application —
-- src:3982 | (i) whether the PACC application was based on material
-- src:3983 | (being evidence or legal arguments) that, even with
-- src:3984 | reasonable diligence, could not have been adduced in
-- src:3985 | court before the relevant date;
-- src:3987 | (ii) whether there was any delay in filing the application
-- src:3988 | for PACC permission after the PACP or counsel for
-- src:3989 | the PACP obtained the material mentioned in
-- src:3990 | sub‑paragraph (i) and the reasons for the delay; and
-- src:3992 | (iii) whether the PACP has complied with
-- src:3993 | section 60H(2);
-- src:3995 | (c) in relation to an application for review permission —
-- src:3997 | (i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions
-- src:3998 | or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K
-- src:3999 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:4001 | (ii) whether the application for review permission was
-- src:4002 | filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or
-- src:4003 | counsel for the PACP had obtained the material
-- src:4004 | mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal
-- src:4005 | Procedure Code 2010; and
-- src:4007 | (iii) whether the PACP has complied with
-- src:4008 | section 394H(3) of the Criminal Procedure
-- src:4009 | Code 2010;
-- src:4016 | (d) in relation to a review application —
-- src:4018 | (i) whether the PACP has complied with the conditions
-- src:4019 | or the requirements in sections 394G, 394J and 394K
-- src:4020 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010;
-- src:4022 | (ii) whether the application for review permission
-- src:4023 | granted in respect of the review application was
-- src:4024 | filed within a reasonable time after the PACP or
-- src:4025 | counsel for the PACP had obtained the material
-- src:4026 | mentioned in section 394J(2) of the Criminal
-- src:4027 | Procedure Code 2010; and
-- src:4029 | (iii) whether the PACP has complied with section 394I(2)
-- src:4030 | of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010.
@ref s 60M(2) (src:3955-4030)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 60M(2) kind of application`
      matter IS A `s 60M(2) matter`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(2) the Court of Appeal may inquire into and take into account the matter` MEANS
    IF elem matter (`s 60M(2) the matters that the Court of Appeal may take into account for the kind of application` kind)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may inquire into and take into account the following matters" does not close the list with "only"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:4032 | (3) Despite section 50(1), where a relevant application is heard
-- src:4033 | before a single Judge of the Court of Appeal, a finding under
-- src:4034 | subsection (1) may be made by that Judge.
@ref s 60M(3) (src:4032-4034)
GIVEN `a relevant application is heard before a single Judge of the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(3) a finding under subsection (1) may be made by that Judge despite section 50(1)` MEANS
    IF `a relevant application is heard before a single Judge of the Court of Appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a relevant application is heard before a single Judge of the Court of Appeal" -- the "where" is not met
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:4039 | (a) where the relevant application is being heard by a single
-- src:4040 | Judge of the Court of Appeal — take such evidence itself;
-- src:4041 | or
@ref s 60M(4)(a) (src:4039-4041)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Judges hearing the relevant application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(4)(a) the Court of Appeal may take the evidence itself where a single Judge hears the relevant application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it thinks additional evidence is necessary" -- the "if" is not met
        IF NOT `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence is necessary` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of Judges hearing the relevant application` EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) where the relevant application is being heard by a single Judge of the Court of Appeal" -- the "where" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:4043 | (b) where the relevant application is being heard by 3 or any
-- src:4044 | greater uneven number of Judges sitting in the Court of
-- src:4045 | Appeal — either take such evidence itself or have such
-- src:4046 | evidence taken by one of those Judges.
@ref s 60M(4)(b) (src:4043-4046)
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of Judges hearing the relevant application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60M(4)(b) the Court of Appeal may either take the evidence itself or have it taken by one of the Judges` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if it thinks additional evidence is necessary" -- the "if" is not met
        IF NOT `the Court of Appeal thinks additional evidence is necessary` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the number of Judges hearing the relevant application` AT LEAST 3 AND (`the number of Judges hearing the relevant application` MODULO 2) EQUALS 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) where the relevant application is being heard by 3 or any greater uneven number of Judges" -- the "where" is not met
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
